<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's South Eastern tries to mop up BOP shares.</title>
<headline>NZ's South Eastern tries to mop up BOP shares.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Eastern Utilities Limited said on Friday it was offering NZ$7.30 per share to small shareholders in Bay of Plenty Electricity Limited.</p>
<p>In a statement SEU said it would pay $7.30 and there would be no brokerage charge to holders of fewer than 5,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746, fax 4736 212</p>
